// Work that FOLLOWS a discard must not be silently dropped (t_72810bd7).
//
// The default path is a shape matcher and enumerates exactly one
// post-discard shape.  This lerp is not it, so the whole statement was
// skipped: the shader compiled, exited 0, printed nothing, and rendered
// the colour unfogged.  The container was well formed and its input mask
// correctly described the ucode - which was missing a line of the source.
//
// Reduced from build/shader-corpus/th06-ps3/files/ps3/shaders/th06_notex.fcg.
//
// The requirement flipped twice, as each item said it would.  While the
// lerp was not a shape either path lowered, a REFUSAL was the required
// behaviour - compiling meant shipping a shader missing a line of its
// source.  c157570 lowered it on the default path, and CF-2
// (t_91bbd575) lowers the discard on the general path, so the
// requirement now is the strong one on BOTH paths: the shader compiles,
// the kill is emitted, and the work after it survives.  The reference
// puts the KIL mid-program and leaves what follows unpredicated - a kill
// is not a terminator.
void main(float4 color : TEXCOORD0,
          float4 fog   : TEXCOORD2,
          out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    if (color.a < 0.0157) discard;
    float4 c = color;
    c.xyz = fog.xyz + (c.xyz - fog.xyz) * fog.w;   /* lerp(fogColor, c, coef) */
    oColor = c;
}
